{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Howzit, come through. What can I do for you today?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Hey. So my skin's been breaking out and my periods are all over the show, both for like two years now. I kept thinking it would just sort itself out.",
  "[SEG0003] person_2 (PATIENT): Eish, and the parking by the robots was mad, we nearly missed you. Anyway.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Doctor, she's put on weight as well, and there's hair on her chin. I've been telling her to come for months.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag, the hair is just a little bit on the chin, not a beard or anything. The weight, ja, my jeans are tighter, but it's not hectic. Periods come every two or three months.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (CAREGIVER): And the cramps are terrible when it does come. She lies in bed the whole day.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): No, aunty, that's not right. I don't get terrible cramps. They're not sore. I just spot for ages, like ten days, brown at the end, and it's annoying.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok, so I'm hearing irregular cycles for two years, long spotting, acne, a little chin hair and some weight gain. I'm thinking this may be polycystic ovary syndrome, a working impression rather than a firm diagnosis. Bloods and a pelvic scan will tell us more.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Yoh. My mom has diabetes, the sugar kind, she's been on tablets for years. Is this that?",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Not the same illness. PCOS can affect sugars down the line though, so your mom's diabetes is worth knowing, and I'll check a fasting glucose.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fevers with this?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No fever.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any cough, or feeling short of breath?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No, chest is fine. I walk up to campus most days. Well, not if it's raining, then I uber, but ja no cough.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Headaches, or any funny vision?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm not really headaches. My eyes get tired if I'm on the laptop till one, but that's assignments, not a headache headache.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll leave that. Are you on any medicines right now?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh the chemist by the robot at Campus Square knows me hey. I get the tea tree wash, my flatmate says it smells like a braai, and we did have a braai Saturday, smoke in my hair, hectic.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, I meant tablets or prescribed creams. Anything like that?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh. Ja. Benzoyl peroxide gel, five percent, I put it on the spots at night. And the GP gave me doxicycline last year, a hundred milligrams once a day, but I stopped after about three weeks. My stomach was not lekker.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She doesn't put the gel on every night though. She falls asleep on her phone.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Err, I do most nights. I skip maybe one or two. Not like I forget the whole week.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Alright, a bit hit and miss then. Any burning when you pass urine?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): When the period finally comes the spotting goes brown. Is brown normal, or is that old blood?",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Different question, we'll park that. Burning or pain when you wee?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh. No, wee's fine. Sorry, I go off on one.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sharp. Thursday morning the nurse will take fasting bloods, be here at eight. Nothing to eat or drink except water from about ten the night before. I'll do glucose, testosterone, LH, FSH, and a thyroid test.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Thursday I've got a tut at ten. Eight is fine, I'll make it.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Good. I've also booked a pelvic ultrasound for next Wednesday at the scan department. It's the internal scan, so you don't need a full bladder.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): If that fasting glucose comes back borderline, then we do a glucose tolerance test. I'm not arranging that one now. A combined contraceptive pill can help cycles and skin, but I'm not starting it today. We'll only look at it once the bloods and the scan are back.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok. My cousin is on the pill for her skin and she says it's lekker, but ja, wait for the tests.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come back and see me in two weeks. Keep the gel on most nights if you can, and the walking you're already doing is worth keeping up.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Sharp, thanks doc. We'll pitch on Thursday."
 ],
